# CODEOWNERS - ROUTING AND NOTIFICATION. IT IS NOT A SECURITY CONTROL.
#
# Honest verdict after reading the official docs, because pretending otherwise
# would be worse than not having the file:
#
#   This repo belongs to a PERSONAL ACCOUNT and has ONE human with write
#   permission. In that scenario "Require review from Code Owners" adds no
#   security; it adds two ways to get stuck:
#     - on the owner's own PRs it is an unsatisfiable block (the author of a
#       PR does not count as an approver, and nobody else has write), and
#     - on the knowledge bot's PRs it demands a human click, which is
#       exactly what automatic promotion exists to remove.
#   That is why branches.main.protection.require_code_owner_reviews = false in
#   scripts/gh/governance.json, and apply-governance.sh verifies it every time.
#
# So what is this file for? For the one thing that DOES work without branch
# protection: the docs say code owners "are automatically requested for review
# when someone opens a pull request that modifies code that they own".
# That is, automatic and targeted notification.
# Translated to this repo: if the knowledge loop (or anyone) opens a PR that
# touches the indirect injection surface, the owner gets a named review
# request instead of having to watch the PR list.
#
# Where the REAL control lives:
#   - the executable gates in scripts/gates/ (rc 0/1/2, where rc=0 never means
#     "I did not review it"),
#   - the independent verifier over the diff,
#   - the 7-day quarantine before promoting to stable,
#   - and the path allowlist that stops an automated PR from touching .github/,
#     scripts/ or .claude-plugin/.
# CODEOWNERS is the bell, not the lock.
#
# Syntax: .gitignore style. The LAST matching pattern wins, so the order goes
# from general to specific. Negation with "!" does NOT work here (documented
# GitHub limitation); do not use it.
# Every owner listed must have write permission or GitHub ignores the line.

